<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Phase 787 — the boundary that stops the repository-wide MSBuild walk at
    the generated oracle. Phase 1037 — and states the Phase 624
    incomplete-match rule itself, so the boundary is no longer an
    exemption from it.

    **It deliberately does NOT import the parent.** MSBuild walks up from a
    project directory until it finds a `Directory.Build.props` and stops
    there unless that file imports its own parent; this one does not, so
    the repo-root props never reaches the extractions. That is the same
    structural mechanism `templates/safer/` and
    `templates/platformsdk-solution/` use. The walk stops because
    everything under this directory is the prover's output, not authored
    code: the root props is the policy for packages this repository
    publishes (version, package metadata, readme and icon, XML docs), and
    none of it describes a generated, unpackable proof oracle.

    FS0025 IS AN ERROR HERE (Phase 1037). The root props promotes FS0025
    to an error tree-wide (Phase 624); this file states the same promotion
    below, so the oracle is under the rule exactly as authored code is, and
    `ArchitectureFitness.fs0025ExemptPrefixes` no longer names this
    subtree. Until Phase 1035 that was impossible: the F* extractor emits
    one field projector per constructor argument, each a single-case
    `match` over a multi-case union, and nobody can fix a file a byte-diff
    holds identical to the extractor's output. Since 1035
    `normalise-extraction.fsx` completes each such match with one explicit,
    loudly failing arm per missing case — the root policy's own
    prescription for an unreachable case — and since 1037 `check.ps1`
    strips the FS0025 suppression Custard's backend writes into its
    `#nowarn` line, so every committed extraction compiles with the rule
    on. A future extraction shape the normaliser does not complete now
    fails BOTH the proof leg's build and the solution build, by name,
    rather than compiling into a silent warning.

    WHAT IS LOST by not importing the root, so nobody has to re-derive it:
    the package metadata and version guarded on `IsPackable != false`, and
    `GenerateDocumentationFile`. Every project here is `IsPackable=false`
    and sets its own doc-file property. A project added under
    `proofs/oracle/` in future inherits this file rather than the root one
    — which is why nothing but the generated oracle should live here.
-->
<Project>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);FS0025</WarningsAsErrors>
    </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
